 & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 3)i-(2\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot (-1))j+(2\\cdot 3-(-4)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =8i+6j+2k \\\\  & =⟨8,6,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-1,3,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨8,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 8+3\\cdot 6+(-5)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552766 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552767 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552766 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552766 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $a=⟨4,-3,-1⟩,$ $b=⟨-1,-5,-2⟩,$ and $c=⟨-2,-3,-3⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552766 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8e17b30a-856b-5ad3-9fe4-036dbdb66eb5" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552766 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-5)\\cdot (-3)-(-2)\\cdot (-3))i-((-1)\\cdot (-3)-(-2)\\cdot (-2))j+((-1)\\cdot (-3)-(-5)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =9i+j-7k \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨4,-3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨9,1,-7⟩ \\\\  & =4\\cdot 9+(-3)\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552770 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552751 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552770 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552770 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $a=⟨-2,3,-5⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-3,5⟩,$ and $c=⟨-1,1,-2⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552770 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc421905-ccc1-5356-85d1-164c6440e5a1" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552770 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-3)\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot (-1))j+(2\\cdot 1-(-3)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-2,3,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-1)+(-5)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552775 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552771 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552775 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552775 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $a=⟨4,2,-4⟩,$ $b=⟨-3,-1,-4⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,5,-4⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552775 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6f58672-c2d9-5b4b-a1ac-70b06c5419c6" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552775 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-4)-(-4)\\cdot 5)i-((-3)\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot (-4))j+((-3)\\cdot 5-(-1)\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =24i-24j-12k \\\\  & =⟨24,-24,-12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨4,2,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨24,-24,-12⟩ \\\\  & =4\\cdot 24+2\\cdot (-24)+(-4)\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =96-48+48 \\\\  & =96\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552776 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552752 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552776 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552776 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $a=⟨-5,-5,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,-1,-3⟩,$ and $c=⟨5,-3,2⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552776 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e37f57a2-326b-5f48-88f5-0e74cb3e0632" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552776 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-3))i-(1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot (-3))j+(1\\cdot (-3)-(-1)\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =-11i-17j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-11,-17,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-5,-5,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-11,-17,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-11)+(-5)\\cdot (-17)+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =55+85+2 \\\\  & =142\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552778 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186105735.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186552778 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "32b3f2de-a30d-5de0-b591-75f1f73fcece" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186553844 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186554649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553844 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186554656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553844 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186554661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553844 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186554663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186